    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34476" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμπολῑτεύω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be a citizen, hold civil rights</i> in a place,
				<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				4.106
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ἐκεῖ</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				103
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ ἐμπολιτευθέντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Isoc.
					5.5
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῇ πόλει καὶ τοῖς ἐμπολιτευομένοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					5.9.9
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀφροσύνη ἐνεπολίτευσε τῷ ἔθνει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>AJ</u>
					17.10.6
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰς -ομένας ἡδονὰς ἐν Ῥώμῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
					<u>VA</u>
					5.36
				</span></i>
			: —
				Med.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. τῷ βίῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Jul.
					<u>Or.</u>
					4.157b
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμπολιτεύεσθαί τινι</span>
			<i>to talk politics with</i> one, <i><span class="en">
				Cic.
				<u>Att.</u>
				7.7.7
			</span></i> codd. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> trans.,
				<i>introduce into a state, naturalize</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ἀκολασίαν οὐρανῷ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Heraclit.
					<u>All.</u>
					69
				</span></i>
			.</div>
